            "title": "Embraer eyes 100 commercial jet deliveries per year in 2028, CEO says",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "(Reuters) -Embraer expects to reach 100 commercial aircraft deliveries per year in 2028, its CEO told Reuters, adding that supply chain issues will likely keep the Brazilian planemaker from hitting that mark sooner.  It forecasts between 77 and 85 commercial jet deliveries this year, up from 73 in 2024.  CEO Francisco Gomes Neto has warned previously that supply chain snags would limit production plans for Embraer, which last cleared 100 annual commercial jet deliveries in 2017.",
